NOTICE — provenance of the character cameo in "Violet Garden"
=============================================================

This repository hosts a non-commercial web experience. It includes a stylized
cameo of an existing anime character. The following is stated plainly so that no
reader — a platform, a juror, or a rights holder — has to infer it.

WHAT THE CAMEO IS
  A single 3D figure appears at the end of the piece. She was produced by an
  image-to-3D conversion of fan artwork of the character, then rebuilt for this
  scene: the conversion's texture atlas was sampled per source triangle and
  re-baked as per-vertex colour (pipeline/vc_bake_source.cjs), collapsed to
  90,000 triangles in Blender (pipeline/violet_convert.py), and compressed with
  meshopt at 16-bit vertex colour (pipeline/compress.sh).

NO ORIGINALITY IS CLAIMED FOR THE CHARACTER
  Character design, likeness, and the underlying artwork belong to their rights
  holder. This repository does not claim "original character design", does not
  claim original geometry, texture, or artwork for the figure, and does not
  claim a licence of any kind. The figure is a fan tribute.

WHAT IS ORIGINAL TO THIS REPOSITORY
  The garden, the ink-and-type system, the letter beats, the shaders, the
  procedural flora, the writing desk, the grounding, the accessibility layer,
  and all written content are authored for this project. Only the figure's
  likeness and her painted surface derive from third-party source art.

Naming discipline in the product itself: the official franchise title never
appears in <title>, og:title, alt text, ARIA labels, tags, or in-scene
signature — she is signed "the Garden Keeper". The homage is disclosed in
/archive's credits block and here.

